PROP-106 shadow mode flag — created 2026-06-17.

Presence of this file activates SHADOW mode for monitor/scripts/lint-exp-allocations.js:
  - Invariant violations are logged to monitor/integrity/lint-exp-allocations-shadow.jsonl
  - Push is ALLOWED (lint exits 0 even on violation)

To enforce: `git rm monitor/decisions/prop-106-shadow.flag && git commit && git push`
  - Then lint blocks any push that would violate next_id > max(live ∪ archive)
  - or that contains duplicate EXP ids in items[].

Phase 0 → Phase 1 transition criteria (from PROP-106 verification_pattern):
  1. Shadow log accumulates ≥7 days of operation
  2. Zero unexpected SHADOW entries logged (i.e., once the prompt edits stop
     producing stale-write commits, shadow should show zero violations).
  3. analyst-baby + analyst + decider have all run at least one cycle each
     with the updated prompts and successfully passed --verify in their hooks.

